Original commit body from 89cdb06f2fefd963f7b1a1edc47101eafb25bfc2:

Docstring-staleness audit, C bundle (silent omission of substantial new
functionality). Unlike the A+B+D bundle these needed new prose rather than
a deletion, so they ship separately.

sketch_embeddings.py: the one-line claim "These functions fall back
gracefully when sentence-transformers isn't installed" named one failure
mode where there are two, and the omitted one is INV-rupid. Replaced with
an explicit degradation contract: (1) the library is not importable, which
_has_sentence_transformers() answers and ONLY answers, and (2) the library
imports but the model weights are not on disk and cannot be fetched, where
that guard returns True and the load raises EmbeddingsUnavailable. Records
that all four public entry points handle both, that the warning fires once
per process, and why the probe is deliberately NOT strengthened to demand
weights — a first install legitimately has the library and no weights.

safety_zones.py: "How to use" named 8 wrappers; 22 exist. Now grouped by
zone with the zone-enforced ones marked, plus the repo_inspect_* family,
which the module title ("write wrappers") does not cover at all — these
are subprocess READS, narrowing from repo_inspect_git through
repo_inspect_scan to repo_inspect_probe, which reads nothing whatsoever.

discovery.py: content-conditioned virtualenv exclusion was undocumented.
venv/.venv/env are deliberately absent from DEFAULT_EXCLUDES because a
directory is a virtualenv by what it CONTAINS, not what it is called.
Carries the disclosed limit forward: the Windows marker arm has zero
real-world positives across the 467-repo corpus and is fixture-asserted.

Docstring text only — no behavior change, no test changes. 15087 passed.

